# BuildTwin Drone Navigation — Definition of Done

Paths below resolve from the repository root. Read `AGENTS.md` and the canonical
constitution at `../buildtwin/.specify/memory/constitution.md` before work. Follow its compatibility,
test-first, data-preservation, and evidence rules; report conflicts and preserve unrelated changes.

See also: `.cursor/rules/sprint-implementation.mdc` | `../buildtwin/docs/SPRINT-WORKFLOW.md`

Do **not** mark a task complete until all applicable checks pass:

## Drone Navigation

- `ruff check .` — lint zero errors
- `python -m pytest tests/ -v` — all tests green
- CI coverage gate: 70% on `app` + `navigation`

## Honest status

Report: code done / tests pass / lint pass — separately.

Required failed or blocked checks prevent a completion claim. Record actual commands, versions,
configuration, results, evidence, and limitations; builds, health, mocks, and HTTP 200 alone are
not journey acceptance. Apply the canonical workflow
(`../buildtwin/docs/SPRINT-WORKFLOW.md`) for affected journeys and CI gaps.
